{
  "notes": [
    "Tongue and groove boards (mitcad#477): Mitcad's own parametric sections of industry-standard sizes, no supplier and no manufacturer's drawing. Sizes are thickness x width in mm (the actual size, the width over the tongue); the cover width (the width a board covers in a floor or a wall) is a row's own, the width less its tongue's length.",
    "The section: the tongue (length TL, thickness TT, its centre TO from the board's middle) on the +X edge, a groove 1 mm (GC) deeper and 0.5 mm (GW) wider than the tongue on the -X edge, the visible face towards +Y. Panel boards have a V-joint: the face edges chamfered by VB at the angle VA to the face. The sizes and covers are those of public product lists; the tongue's and groove's sizes are Mitcad's own.",
    "Species: floorboards pine, panel boards spruce. Densities at 20 % moisture: spruce 450 kg/m3, pine 520 kg/m3 (grounds in timber-sawn.json's notes).",
    "Tolerances (planed): thickness up to 20 mm +-0.5 mm, over 20 mm +-1.0 mm; width up to 100 mm +-1.0 mm, over 100 mm +-1.5 mm."
